LayerStack shows the layers of one system (field instruments up to the plant network) as an exploded isometric stack of machined plates, each carrying its equipment, with the labels on leaders from the plate corners.

Look `layer-stack` (`assets/src/blocks/look-layer-stack.js`) on a `diagram` block. Used on sys-monitoring, "How the controls are built". Concept adapted: home.3 (exploded part view with leader callouts), recast as a soft render of plates (tonal faces, no drawing sheet).

- Markup: `<div class="aq-layer-stack" data-at="…" style="--ls-zoom;--ls-shift">` > `__fig` (one `svg.aq-layer-stack__svg`: per stage a `g.__layer` with `g.__plate` (`__front`, `__side`, `__top`, `__inset`, `__hole`), `g.__eqp` (IsoKit parts and inline line art) and `__trace`; `g.__gap` risers between plates; `__axis`; `g.__lead` per label; `__route` (hidden) and `__packet`) + `ol.__list` of `li.__item(--r|--l)` (index, `h3.__t`, `p.__d`) positioned over the figure at percentages the renderer computed.
- Stages draw bottom up: the first stage is the lowest plate, each next one higher and further back; labels alternate right (even) and left (odd).
- Fields: `stages [{t, d, icon, art, key}]`, `caption`. `art`: `instruments` (three analysers on a process pipe), `plc` (rack of I/O modules on a backplate), `hmi` (operator panel on a pedestal with a trend), `historian` (server rack and three drums), `network` (switch, dashed DMZ boundary with firewall, cable out); default by position. `key: true` draws that plate navy (the controller that keeps running when every layer above fails).
- Tokens: plates `surface-raised` top, `line` / `line-strong` mixes for front and side, `navy` for the key plate; signal and packet `flow`; labels `ink` / `ink-muted`, leaders `line-strong`.
- Drawn inline (not in IsoKit): the plates, the PLC rack, the HMI screen, the historian rack and drums, the network switch, firewall and DMZ. Analysers and pipes are IsoKit.
- Phones: the svg is zoomed to the stack (`--ls-zoom`, `--ls-shift` from the renderer) and the labels list under it in stage order.
- Not for a flow of process stages (use WindingRoute or StrataRun) or more than six layers.

Motion: the plates arrive pressed together and lift apart to their places, lowest first; equipment settles onto each, risers and axis appear, water runs the instrument pipe, leaders draw and labels slide in from their side; then one packet rides the data route from the instruments to the plant network, lighting each plate's leader and label as it passes (they settle after). Once, under 5 s. Hover a label to light its plate.
